* START-HISTORY:
* 22 Oct 26 dm  New (S.75, H2; the owner: "a terminal session that can be ended with exit").
* 7 Nov 26 dm   S.164: /tkhome/ has a fourth variable, hrefused (declared alike everywhere).
* 10 Nov 26 dm  S.201: a screen typed at the prompt stays one after the Terminal tile and EXIT (hflag 2); it was made the session's own, and Ctrl-Q then signed out.
* END-HISTORY
*
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
*   EXIT
*
*   When the person left the home screen by its Terminal tile (the flag hflag of the named common /TKHOME/, set by HOME), starts HOME again: its Terminal tile
*   brings them back to this prompt, and EXIT to the screen.  Otherwise it does what QUIT does and ends the session.  A command processor cannot be nested, so
*   the terminal is the ordinary prompt and EXIT is the way back; the flag stays set for the rest of the session.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
program $exit
$catalog $exit

   common /tkhome/ hflag, hlogto, hstart, hrefused

   if hflag and @tty[1, 5] = '/dev/' then
      hstart = (hflag = 1)                     ;* 10 Nov 26 (S.201): back from the Terminal tile, the screen is what it was before the tile was used: the session's own (1) or typed at the prompt (2)
      execute 'home'
   end else
      execute 'quit'
   end

end

* END-CODE
